uuidd: preserve double-fork daemonization with callback clone on wasm

musl's daemon() is fork-based and unavailable.  Recreate the daemon(0, 0)
sequence (redirect, detach session, reparent) with private-memory callback
clones.  The service loop body moves to server_loop_service so the daemon
continuation can start there; signalfd handling stays native.

